#!/bin/bash

cat <<'EOF'
STARTUP CHECKLIST - Apply the current user request and project policies:

EXECUTION: Direct implementation, tests, git and worktree management are permitted. Use specialists when the task and applicable routing call for them; do not turn every action into mandatory delegation. Foreground user-directed work does not grant authority over unrelated autonomous work.
OWNERSHIP: Resolve installed links and native formats before editing. Reusable framework content belongs in common/ plus tool overlays; organization overrides retain their private owner and host dotfiles only wire them.
PLANS: Keep plans/specs untracked in the current checkout's designated planning directory. Never force-add or publish them. Do not impose a separate documentation repository as a universal plan location.
DISPATCH: Read the installed agent definition; preserve its declared model, effort, tools and authority. Use paths rather than copied context. Independent authorized dispatches can run concurrently; uncertain runs need their original terminal identity before retry.
COMMUNICATIONS: Draft external messages and obtain explicit approval before posting. The standing exception is opening a draft PR through the project's prescribed workflow. Do not mark ready, assign reviewers, merge or deploy without authorization.
JIRA: Use TWG first, including transition discovery and required fields. Fall back only when unavailable or missing an operation; report unsupported required fields rather than guessing.
VERIFICATION: Run focused checks for touched files and retain actual results. A cache, startup snapshot or unavailable analyzer is not evidence of health. Prefer native code intelligence where available.
EOF
